From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:19:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] scl: placement side-file support for placement-aware
 sizing

New read_place/print_place/reset_place commands (sclPlace.c): load
net-name-keyed cell coordinates (ports as <name>@pin for die pins);
Abc_SclAddWireLoad then uses exact HPWL wire caps instead of the
fanout-count wire-load table (per-net fallback when a coordinate is
missing), enabled even without a liberty wire_load group. Scl_Con
(read_constr -n) boundary budgets now reach the Abc_Ntk STA: PI
arrivals offset CI times, PO requireds seed CO-driver departures.
Placement survives topo via Scl_PlaceTransfer (DupDfs drops node
names). Also fixes read_constr's -n flag, which toggled fVerbose
instead of the new-format switch, leaving the Scl_Con path dead.

Units are SCL-internal (fF/um, kOhm/um); smoke-verified on a long
single-sink net: the wire cap reaches the load, and upsize responds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
